      "writtenOn": "2024-07-23T18:26:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(a) A patch to make the private constructor (in line 153 I understand) protected would be fine.\n\n(b) Yeah, I think if we wrap epoll_ctl() then indeed epoll_wait() on the externally visible epoll fd will quite likely return the event causing fd.  That seems to be unavoidable...  Technically that would require wrapping epoll_wait() as well, but that seems infeasible [think of trying to simultaneously wait on 2 different bpf ringbuffers]... so I think epoll_wait() has to remain external to the class.  At best we can provide some sort of \u0027bool isThisYourEpollEvent(epoll_event)\u0027 helper... though not sure if that is even needed... since you could always just call ConsumeAll on any and all BpfRingBuffers any time you\u0027re woken up and can\u0027t recognize the fd.",
